  "correction_rules": [
    "When sentiment is negative (≤ 0.00), reduce forecasted prices by 5–10% to account for downward pressure.",
    "After a price spike (forecast > 70.00), apply a 3–5 day lag correction: reduce forecast by 2–5% per day to avoid overshoot.",
    "If true outcome is consistently below forecast (persistent underperformance), apply mean reversion: adjust forecast toward recent 5-day average.",
    "For sentiment > 0.50, increase forecast by 3–7% to reflect bullish momentum, but cap at 75.00 to avoid overestimation.",
    "If forecast is > 75.00 and true outcome is < 65.00, apply downward bias correction: reduce by 10–15% to reflect market correction.",
    "In early stages of price decline (sentiment negative but price > 65.00), apply gradual decay: reduce forecast by 1–2% per day until price stabilizes."
  ]
}
